h \r\n Suomeksi \r\n Auf Deutsch \r\n Français \r\n En español \r\n In italiano \r\n Русский \r\n 日本語 \r\n 中文 \r\n باللغة العربية \r\n Activate listen \n SV \n Enter search terms \n Search \n Search \n Menu \n Drottningholm Palace \n Startsida \n English \n Royal palaces and sites \n Drottningholm Palace \n Share \n Language \n På svenska \n In English \n Suomeksi \n Auf Deutsch \n Français \n En español \n In italiano \n Русский \n 日本語 \n 中文 \n باللغة العربية \n Activate listen\n Samtycke för funktionella kakor\n För att använda lyssnafunktionen behöver du lämna ditt samtycke till funktionella kakor.\n Samtyck till funktionella kakor\n Avbryt\n Drottningholm Palace\n Drottningholm Palace is on UNESCO&#39;s World Heritage list. It is the most well-preserved royal castle built in the 1600s in Sweden and at the same time is representative of all European architecture for the period.\n Make a day trip to Drottningholm and experience a historic milieu of the highest international standards. The combination of the exotic Chinese Pavilion pleasure palace, the palace theatre and the magnificent palace gardens make a visit to Drottningholm a unique experience.\n Influenced by French prototype, the palace was built by architect Nicodemus Tessin the Elder by commission of Queen Hedvig Eleonora. A number of royal personages have since then left their mark on the palace.\n The Palace is Their Majesties the King and Queen&#39;s permanent home residence. The rooms in the southern wing of the palace are reserved for this purpose. The rest of the palace and grounds are open to the public year round.\n History and highlights of Drottningholm Palace \n Photo: Raphael Stecksén/Royalpalaces.se \n Tickets \n Opening hours \r\n Calendar \r\n Visit us \r\n Guided tours \n App with guides \n Childrens Drottningholm \n Group Visits \n Admission charges \n Getting here \n Practical information, Access \n Travel companies and authorised guides \n Contact us \n Discover more at Drottningholm P