indow.open(","Instagram"],["javascript:void(window.open(","Youtube"],["https://www.royalpalaces.se/english/about-the-site/cookie-policy.html","Cookie policy"],["https://www.royalpalaces.se/english/about-the-site/personal-data.html","Personal data"],["https://www.royalpalaces.se/english/about-the-site.html","About the website"],["https://www.royalpalaces.se/english/image-and-media-gallery.html","Image and Media Gallery"],["https://www.kungligaslotten.se/om-webbplatsen/policy-for-kakor/aktivera-funktionen-for-vanliga-fragor-faq.html",""]]},"https://www.royalpalaces.se/english/royal-palaces-and-sites/rosendal-palace.html":{"status":200,"final":"https://www.royalpalaces.se/english/royal-palaces-and-sites/rosendal-palace.html","title":"Rosendal Palace - Kungliga slotten","text":"Rosendal Palace - Kungliga slotten \n Skip to page content \n The Royal Palaces \n Share \n Language \r\n På svenska \r\n In English \r\n Suomeksi \r\n Auf Deutsch \r\n Français \r\n En español \r\n In italiano \r\n Русский \r\n 日本語 \r\n 中文 \r\n باللغة العربية \r\n Activate listen \n SV \n Enter search terms \n Search \n Search \n Menu \n Rosendal Palace \n Startsida \n English \n Royal palaces and sites \n Rosendal Palace \n Share \n Language \n På svenska \n In English \n Suomeksi \n Auf Deutsch \n Français \n En español \n In italiano \n Русский \n 日本語 \n 中文 \n باللغة العربية \n Activate listen\n Samtycke för funktionella kakor\n För att använda lyssnafunktionen behöver du lämna ditt samtycke till funktionella kakor.\n Samtyck till funktionella kakor\n Avbryt\n Rosendal Palace\n Rosendal Palace on Djurgården in Stockholm is a unique document of the Swedish Empire style, also known as the Karl Johan style. Rosendal was a summer palace where members of the royal family could come to escape the formalities of courtly life in the city.\n Rosendal Palace is located at the Djurgården hunting park and was built in the 1820s for King Karl XIV Johan, the first Bernadotte.\n Rosendal was originally a summertime pleasure retreat. It has never been a residence in the modern sense of the word. It was merely intended as an escape from the formalities of court life at the Royal Palace.\n One of the leading architects of the time, Fredrik Blom, received a royal commission to draw and build the palace building. The building was produced in the fashion of a prefabricated house.\n The palace stands today largely as it did in Karl Johan&#39;s lifetime, which makes Rosendal a unique documentation of the European Empire style, in Sweden also known as the Karl Johan style.\n Photo: Raphael Stecksén/Royalpalaces.se \n Tickets \n Opening hours \r\n Visit us \r\n Guided tours \n Group Visits \n Getting here \n Admission charges \n Practical information, Access \n Souvenirs \n Contact us \n Discover more at Rosendal Palace \r\n Rosendal Palace Halls \n The Palace Park \n History \n Sculpture Park \n Royal Djurgården \n National City Park \n Visit us\n Guided tours \n Join a guided tour and hear about the palace’s royal history, the history of the buildi...\n Group Visits \n Advance bookings are recommended for larger groups. Rosendal Palace can open for booked...\n Getting here \n Discover more at Rosendal Palace\n Rosendal Palace Halls \n The palace remains largely unchanged since the time of King Karl Johan and King Oskar, ...\n The Palace Park \n Explore the buildings at Rosendal that King Karl XIV Johan had built in the 19th centur...\n Rosendal Palace's History \n Rosendal Palace was built on southern Djurgården in 1823-27 for King Karl XIV Johan ....\n The Sculpture Park \n The Spanish artist Cristina Iglesias has been commissioned to create the seventh perman...\n Royal Djurgården \n Royal Djurgården is Stockholm's most popular recreation area. The area is unique in ter...\n The Royal National City Park \n King Carl XVI Gustaf officially opened Sweden's first National City Park in 1995 , comp...\n Articles and movies\n Autumn at the Royal palaces \n Explore three royal site