avascript:void(window.open(","Youtube"],["https://www.royalpalaces.se/english/about-the-site/cookie-policy.html","Cookie policy"],["https://www.royalpalaces.se/english/about-the-site/personal-data.html","Personal data"],["https://www.royalpalaces.se/english/about-the-site.html","About the website"],["https://www.royalpalaces.se/english/image-and-media-gallery.html","Image and Media Gallery"],["https://www.kungligaslotten.se/om-webbplatsen/policy-for-kakor/aktivera-funktionen-for-vanliga-fragor-faq.html",""]]},"https://www.royalpalaces.se/english/royal-palaces-and-sites/ulriksdal-palace.html":{"status":200,"final":"https://www.royalpalaces.se/english/royal-palaces-and-sites/ulriksdal-palace.html","title":"Ulriksdal Palace - Kungliga slotten","text":"Ulriksdal Palace - Kungliga slotten \n Skip to page content \n The Royal Palaces \n Share \n Language \r\n På svenska \r\n In English \r\n Suomeksi \r\n Auf Deutsch \r\n Français \r\n En español \r\n In italiano \r\n Русский \r\n 日本語 \r\n 中文 \r\n باللغة العربية \r\n Activate listen \n SV \n Enter search terms \n Search \n Search \n Menu \n Ulriksdal Palace \n Startsida \n English \n Royal palaces and sites \n Ulriksdal Palace \n Share \n Language \n På svenska \n In English \n Suomeksi \n Auf Deutsch \n Français \n En español \n In italiano \n Русский \n 日本語 \n 中文 \n باللغة العربية \n Activate listen\n Samtycke för funktionella kakor\n För att använda lyssnafunktionen behöver du lämna ditt samtycke till funktionella kakor.\n Samtyck till funktionella kakor\n Avbryt\n Ulriksdal Palace\n Ulriksdal Palace is situated on the banks of Edsviken Lake in the National City Park in Stockholm. The palace was built in the 1600s and visitors witness many different epochs.\n The palace area of Ulriksdal has a lot to offer. Join the guided tour of the palace, admire the sculptures in the Orangery.\n A tour of Ulriksdal Palace gives the visitor an exciting view of interior design spanning from the 1600s to the 1900s. Several of the rooms on show were created for Karl XV by Fredrik W. Sholander.\n Several Swedish regents have left their mark on Ulriksdal. Queen Kristina built a pleasure garden in front of the palace and Hedvig Elenora built an Orangery in the park. Queen Kristina enjoyed the palace so much that she let her coronation procession proceed from Ulriksdal.\n The palace was built for Constable of the Realm Jacob De La Gardie by architect Hans Jacob Kristler. The palace was called Jacobsdal until the time of Queen Hedvig Eleonora.\n Both the palace and the Orangery are open to the public during the summer months. At the Orangery an exhibition of Swedish sculpture from the Swedish National Museum&#39;s collection can be viewed.\n Photo: Raphael Stecksén/Royalpalaces.se \n Tickets \n Opening hours \r\n Visit us \r\n Guided tours \n App with guides \n Childrens Ulriksdal \n Group Visits \n Getting here \n Admission charges \n Practical information, Access \n Souvenirs \n Contact us \n Discover more at Ulriksdal Palace \r\n The Palace \n The Orangery Museum \n Visitor Centre/Café \n The Royal Gift Shop \n The Theatre Confidencen \n Ulriksdal Palace Chapel \n Ulriksdal Palace Park \n History \n Visit us\n Guided tours \n Join the guided tours and hear about the palace’s royal history, the history of the bui...\n App with guides \n The Swedish Royal Palaces app includes a number of features to enhance your visit to th...\n Childrens Ulriksdal \n Go on a journey of discovery through the rooms and halls of Ulriksdal Palace. The pictu...\n Events\n Ulriksdal's Autumn Market \n 23 – 25 Oct \n For three days in October, Ulriksdal's beautiful Palace Park will be filled with exquis...\n To the calendar \n Discover more at Ulriksdal Palace\n Ulriksdal Palace Halls \n A tour of Ulriksdal Palace gives the visitor an exciting view of interior design spanni...\n The Orangery Museum \n Centrally located in the Ulriksdal Palace grounds beside the palace itself lies the gre...\n Ulriksdal Visitor Centre and ca